# Jetpack areas and the areas each one may use (direct dependencies only; the harness adds the closure).
# Each area is checked as its own unit containing only itself and its dependency closure, so an area
# cannot reach code it did not declare. Layers mirror the Rust crates: models (L1/L2) below the engine
# (L3) below the CLI. When cross-package enums, type imports and dependency check reuse work (Tower
# #3673, #3661), each area becomes a package.jet with exactly these dependency edges.
#
# Format: `Area: Dep, Dep` (an area with no dependencies ends with `:`). Order is bottom-up.

Compiler hash:
Compiler front end: Compiler hash
Compiler store: Compiler front end
Foundation: Compiler front end
TrustRoot: Foundation
NixEval:
PackageModel: Foundation
EnvModel: PackageModel, Compiler front end
Nix: NixEval, PackageModel
Store: PackageModel, TrustRoot, Compiler store
Trust: Store, EnvModel
Recipe: Trust
Provider: Trust, Recipe, Nix, EnvModel
Publication: PackageModel, Provider
Environment: Provider
Services: Environment
Image: Environment
JetOS: PackageModel, EnvModel, Store
CLI: Services, Image
